\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15.1}{\ignorespaces The put seller's profit at expiry in the worked example. Above the strike of 100 the seller keeps the \$2.14 premium; below the break-even of 97.86 the loss grows one for one with the fall. A 10\% fall costs \$7.86, about seventeen months of expected gains.}}{197}{figure.caption.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:14-put}{{15.1}{197}{The put seller's profit at expiry in the worked example. Above the strike of 100 the seller keeps the \$2.14 premium; below the break-even of 97.86 the loss grows one for one with the fall. A 10\% fall costs \$7.86, about seventeen months of expected gains}{figure.caption.61}{}}
